<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 7.2 Exercises</heading>
    <paragraph>Solve the following equations using the method of undetermined coefficients.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="54" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$2y^{''} - 5y^{\prime} - 12y = 6$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="55" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$3y^{''} + y^{\prime} - 4y = 8$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 e -4 x / 3 + c 2 e x - 2 y = c 1 e -4 x / 3 + c 2 e x - 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="56" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 6y^{\prime} + 5y = e^{-x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="57" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 16y = e^{-2x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 cos 4 x + c 2 sin 4 x + 1 20 e -2 x y = c 1 cos 4 x + c 2 sin 4 x + 1 20 e -2 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="58" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 4y = x^{2} + 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="59" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 4y^{\prime} + 4y = 8x^{2} + 4x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 e 2 x + c 2 x e 2 x + 2 x 2 + 5 x + 4 y = c 1 e 2 x + c 2 x e 2 x + 2 x 2 + 5 x + 4$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="60" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 2y^{\prime} - 3y = \sin 2x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="61" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 2y^{\prime} + y = \sin x + \cos x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 e - x + c 2 x e - x + 1 2 sin x - 1 2 cos x y = c 1 e - x + c 2 x e - x + 1 2 sin x - 1 2 cos x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="62" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 9y = e^{x}\cos x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="63" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + y = 3\sin 2x + x\cos 2x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 cos x + c 2 sin x - 1 3 x cos 2 x - 5 9 sin 2 x y = c 1 cos x + c 2 sin x - 1 3 x cos 2 x - 5 9 sin 2 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="64" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 3y^{\prime} - 28y = 10e^{4x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="65" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 10y^{\prime} + 25y = xe^{-5x} + 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 e -5 x + c 2 x e -5 x + 1 6 x 3 e -5 x + 4 25 y = c 1 e -5 x + c 2 x e -5 x + 1 6 x 3 e -5 x + 4 25$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In each of the following problems,</paragraph>
    <list type="ordered">
      <item>Write the form for the particular solution $$y_{p}(x)$$ for the method of undetermined coefficients.</item>
      <item>[T] Use a computer algebra system to find a particular solution to the given equation.</item>
    </list>
    <exercise number="66" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - y^{\prime} - y = x + e^{-x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="67" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 3y = x^{2} - 4x + 11$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$yp(x)=Ax2+Bx+Cyp(x)=Ax2+Bx+C$$ b. $$yp(x)=-13x2+43x-359yp(x)=-13x2+43x-359$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="68" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - y^{\prime} - 4y = e^{x}\cos 3x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="69" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$2y^{''} - y^{\prime} + y = \left( {x^{2} - 5x} \right)e^{-x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$yp(x)=(Ax2+Bx+C)e-xyp(x)=(Ax2+Bx+C)e-x$$ b. $$yp(x)=(14x2-58x-3332)e-xyp(x)=(14x2-58x-3332)e-x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="70" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$4y^{''} + 5y^{\prime} - 2y = e^{2x} + x\sin x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="71" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - y^{\prime} - 2y = x^{2}e^{x}\sin x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$yp(x)=(Ax2+Bx+C)excosxyp(x)=(Ax2+Bx+C)excosx$$ $$+(Dx2+Ex+F)exsinx+(Dx2+Ex+F)exsinx$$ b. $$yp(x)=(-110x2-1125x-27250)excosxyp(x)=(-110x2-1125x-27250)excosx$$ $$+(-310x2+225x+39250)exsinx+(-310x2+225x+39250)exsinx$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Solve the differential equation using either the method of undetermined coefficients or the variation of parameters.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="72" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 3y^{\prime} - 4y = 2e^{x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="73" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 2y^{\prime} = e^{3x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 + c 2 e -2 x + 1 15 e 3 x y = c 1 + c 2 e -2 x + 1 15 e 3 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="74" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 6y^{\prime} + 9y = e^{-x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="75" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 2y^{\prime} - 8y = 6e^{2x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 e 2 x + c 2 e -4 x + x e 2 x y = c 1 e 2 x + c 2 e -4 x + x e 2 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Solve the differential equation using the method of variation of parameters.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="76" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$4y^{''} + y = 2\sin x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="77" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 9y = 8x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 e 3 x + c 2 e -3 x - 8 x 9 y = c 1 e 3 x + c 2 e -3 x - 8 x 9$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="78" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + y = \sec x, 0 &lt; x &lt; \pi/2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="79" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + 4y = 3\csc 2x, 0 &lt; x &lt; \pi/2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = c 1 cos 2 x + c 2 sin 2 x - 3 2 x cos 2 x + 3 4 sin 2 x ln ( sin 2 x ) y = c 1 cos 2 x + c 2 sin 2 x - 3 2 x cos 2 x + 3 4 sin 2 x ln ( sin 2 x )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Find the unique solution satisfying the differential equation and the initial conditions given, where $$y_{p}(x)$$ is the particular solution.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="80" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 2y^{\prime} + y = 12e^{x},$$ $$\text{y} _{p}(x) = 6x^{2}e^{x},$$ $$y(0) = 6, y\prime(0) = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="81" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 7y^{\prime} = 4xe^{7x},$$ $$y_{p}(x) = \frac{2}{7}x^{2}e^{7x} - \frac{4}{49}xe^{7x},$$ $$y(0) = -1, y\prime(0) = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = - 347 343 + 4 343 e 7 x + 2 7 x 2 e 7 x - 4 49 x e 7 x y = - 347 343 + 4 343 e 7 x + 2 7 x 2 e 7 x - 4 49 x e 7 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="82" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} + y = \cos x - 4\sin x,$$ $$y_{p}(x) = 2x\cos x + \frac{1}{2}x\sin x,$$ $$y(0) = 8, y\prime(0) = -4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="83" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y^{''} - 5y^{\prime} = e^{5x} + 8e^{-5x},$$ $$y_{p}(x) = \frac{1}{5}xe^{5x} + \frac{4}{25}e^{-5x},$$ $$y(0) = -2, y\prime(0) = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y = - 57 25 + 3 25 e 5 x + 1 5 x e 5 x + 4 25 e -5 x y = - 57 25 + 3 25 e 5 x + 1 5 x e 5 x + 4 25 e -5 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In each of the following problems, two linearly independent solutions— $$y_{1}$$ and $$y_{2}$$ —are given that satisfy the corresponding homogeneous equation. Use the method of variation of parameters to find a particular solution to the given nonhomogeneous equation. Assume x &gt; 0 in each exercise.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="84" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x^{2}y^{''} + 2xy^{\prime} - 2y = 3x,$$ $$y_{1}(x) = x, y_{2}(x) = x^{-2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="85" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x^{2}y^{''} - 2y = 10x^{2} - 1,$$ $$y_{1}(x) = x^{2}, y_{2}(x) = x^{-1}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y p = 1 2 + 10 3 x 2 ln x y p = 1 2 + 10 3 x 2 ln x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
  </exercises>
</section>
